 "title": "Derivatives of Inverse Functions",
 "short": "Derivatives of Inverse Functions",
 "lead": "The <span data-concept=\"derivative\">derivative</span> of an <span data-concept=\"inverse-function\">inverse function</span> is the reciprocal of the derivative of the function at the matching point, the <span data-concept=\"inverse-function-theorem\">inverse function theorem</span>. It extends the <span data-concept=\"power-rule\">power rule</span> to rational exponents and gives the derivatives of the <span data-concept=\"inverse-trigonometric-functions\">inverse trigonometric functions</span>.",
 "objectives": [
  "Calculate the derivative of an inverse function.",
  "Recognize the derivatives of the standard inverse trigonometric functions."
 ],
 "summary_html": "<ul><li>The <span data-concept=\"inverse-function-theorem\">inverse function theorem</span> allows us to compute <span data-concept=\"derivative\">derivatives</span> of <span data-concept=\"inverse-function\">inverse functions</span> without using the <span data-concept=\"limit\">limit</span> definition of the <span data-concept=\"derivative\">derivative</span>.</li><li>We can use the <span data-concept=\"inverse-function-theorem\">inverse function theorem</span> to develop differentiation formulas for the <span data-concept=\"inverse-trigonometric-functions\">inverse trigonometric functions</span>.</li></ul>",
